    {
      "id": "cadences-introduction",
      "title": "Cadences — Introduction",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory | **Tier:** intro | **Difficulty:** 3/10\n**Prerequisites:** Triads — Introduction\n**Tags:** cadences, harmony"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A **cadence** is a harmonic punctuation at a phrase end — the musical equivalent of a comma or full stop."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-types",
      "title": "Common types",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "- **Perfect (authentic)**: V–I (or V7–I) — strong closure\n- **Plagal**: IV–I — \"amen\" cadence\n- **Half**: ends on V — question, continues\n- **Deceptive**: V–vi — surprise, continues"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
